---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { getTranslations } from '../../lib/i18n';

const lang = 'en';
const t = getTranslations(lang);
---

<Layout lang={lang} title="Privacy Policy" description="Our 100% privacy commitment: 0 trackers, 0 third-party cookies, and 0 user profiling on tips.hub.">
  <article class="max-w-4xl mx-auto space-y-8">
    <header class="pb-6 border-b border-[var(--border-color)]">
      <div class="text-xs font-mono font-bold text-[var(--accent)] mb-2">
        $ security --privacy-statement
      </div>
      <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-extrabold text-[var(--text-primary)] tracking-tight mb-3">
        Privacy Policy
      </h1>
      <p class="text-sm text-[var(--text-secondary)] leading-relaxed font-mono">
        tips.hub is built with an absolute privacy-first philosophy: zero trackers, zero tracking cookies, zero ads.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="space-y-6 text-xs sm:text-sm text-[var(--text-secondary)] leading-relaxed font-sans">
      <section class="rounded-xl border border-[var(--border-color)] bg-[var(--bg-surface)] p-6 space-y-3">
        <h2 class="text-base font-bold text-[var(--text-primary)] font-mono">
          # 1. No Personal Data Collection
        </h2>
        <p>
          We require no account registration, no email submissions, and we perform no behavioral profiling on our readers.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="rounded-xl border border-[var(--border-color)] bg-[var(--bg-surface)] p-6 space-y-3">
        <h2 class="text-base font-bold text-[var(--text-primary)] font-mono">
          # 2. Bookmarks are 100% Client-Side
        </h2>
        <p>
          Your saved tips are stored exclusively in your browser's private <code>localStorage</code>. No reading lists are ever transmitted to any remote database.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="rounded-xl border border-[var(--border-color)] bg-[var(--bg-surface)] p-6 space-y-3">
        <h2 class="text-base font-bold text-[var(--text-primary)] font-mono">
          # 3. Privacy-Friendly CDN Metrics
        </h2>
        <p>
          We rely only on standard edge aggregated request counters provided by Cloudflare / Vercel with zero cross-site cookie tracking.
        </p>
      </section>
      <section class="rounded-xl border border-[var(--border-color)] bg-[var(--bg-surface)] p-6 space-y-3">
        <h2 class="text-base font-bold text-[var(--text-primary)] font-mono"># 4. Telegram submissions</h2>
        <p>When you submit through the Telegram bot, the GitHub queue stores your numeric Telegram ID with the link and note for spam limits, status checks, and moderation. Repository maintainers can view the Issue; its visibility follows the repository's public or private settings. The ID is removed from approved website records. Usernames and phone numbers are not stored.</p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </article>
</Layout>
